      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "WF 2a1 - FRAME-BY-FRAME COLMAP DATASET UPSCALE (light on VRAM)\n\nSame job as 2a (upscale an existing SphereSfM COLMAP dataset IN PLACE), but with\nthe 2b1 rail instead of SeedVR2: RealESRGAN_x2 -> pre-sharpen -> Krea2 Turbo tile\nrefine, driven ONE FRAME AT A TIME by a VHS Meta Batch Manager.\n\nWHY USE THIS INSTEAD OF 2a\n- SeedVR2 is a temporal video model: it wants a whole 81-frame sub-video resident\n  on the GPU at once. That is what makes it heavy.\n- This rail is PER-FRAME. Only one face (360px -> 720px at RealESRGAN_x2) is in VRAM, and\n  each finished face is written straight to disk. VRAM cost is roughly 'one Krea2\n  tile', regardless of how many thousand images the dataset has.\n- Trade-off: no temporal consistency model. For cube faces that is mostly fine\n  (denoise is only 0.2, so it sharpens rather than invents), but expect slightly\n  more per-frame variation than SeedVR2 gives. Keep denoise low.\n- Because it is per-frame, CAMERA-MAJOR ORDERING IS IRRELEVANT here. This workflow\n  reads plain lexical order (frame-major) - the same order the filenames sort in -\n  which is why the original filenames map back 1:1.\n\nHOW IT STAYS SAFE (the swap happens UP FRONT, not at the end)\n'Prepare Dataset Upscale' runs BEFORE the loop and does the rename once:\n    images/  ->  images_lowres/     (atomic; the pristine originals, never written to)\n    images/                          recreated EMPTY, ready to be refilled\nThe loader then reads images_lowres/ for the whole loop, and 'Save Upscaled Frames\n(Streaming)' writes each finished face into images/ under its ORIGINAL FILENAME\n(source_names_dir gives it the name list). So sparse/0/images.bin keeps matching.\n\nThe swap CANNOT be done at the end like node 2a does it: the VHS loader resolves all\nits file paths on the first iteration and opens them lazily, so renaming the folder\nmid-loop would make every remaining frame disappear.\n\nIDEMPOTENT: re-running is safe. images_lowres/ already exists -> nothing is renamed,\nthe originals are read from there again and images/ is refilled from scratch.\nCrashed half way? images/ is partially filled, originals are untouched - just re-run.\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. Set 'dataset_name' on Prepare Dataset Upscale to your SphereSfM output_name.\n2. Set the prompt (node 'CLIPTextEncode') to a short scene description.\n3. Tile Size >= the UPSCALED face size (360 faces -> 720 after RealESRGAN_x2, so the\n   preset 1024 covers it) - each face is then a single tile: no seams, no overhead.\n   NOTE: unlike 2a2 this rail goes through the VHS loader, which silently RESIZES any\n   odd-sized image to the majority size instead of erroring. dark-alley-01 has 6 faces\n   at 512x512 and 1938 at 360x360, so frame_00000 would be quietly downsized - fix the\n   dataset first.\n4. Optional resize: 1.00 keeps the clean RealESRGAN 2x. 0.50 lands back at 1x\n   (denoise-only cleanup); 2.00 would take 512 -> 2048.\n5. Queue ONCE. VHS requeues the graph automatically, once per image.\n\nSPEED: it is sequential - one Krea2 pass per face. 1944 faces is a long run, but it\nsaves as it goes, so a crash or a stop only costs the frames not yet written.\n\nThe throwaway VHS_VideoCombine is REQUIRED: VideoHelperSuite only keeps a meta-batch\nloop requeueing while a VHS_VideoCombine sits on the manager. It is fed the cheap\nlow-res frames with save_output=false, so it just advances the loop."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
